t a job  as an Amazon warehouse and I thought  well you know this I was worried that my  book was gonna be boring what am I gonna  I worked in a warehouse before when I  was younger and I was worried it kind of  is he gonna be there boring what I might  what I'm gonna write about it but the  book but pretty much wrote itself as  soon as I as soon as I started the work  there was so many kind of shocking  things going on the  yeah the book essentially wrote itself  so I mean my first job was at Amazon I  kept a diary every day I was working  there and the first day I remember  writing in this diary that the  atmosphere of the Amazon warehouse had  the atmosphere of what I've imagined a  prison would feel like we're saying it's  kind of like hyperbole it sounds like it  sounds like I'm exaggerating but it was  you know you were you were given  discipline reason if you took took days  off sick even with notes from the doctor  you were people were given discipline  teas for taking too long going to the  toilet you got to go through airport  style security every time you went on  break or every time you went to the  toilet so you know taking off your belt  your watch you had to be drug and  alcohol tested there were all these kind  of you you were constantly monitored by  and surveilled by by the management you  were underpaid so we weren't paid the  minimum wage for half the time I was  working there one girl I interviewed was  paid 62 P an hour and it took her six  weeks to get that money back over  Christmas there was all this stuff going  on and my as soon as I got in there my  insensitive reaction was like why does  no one know about this and then it  became then there became then it was  kind of a zeal attached to the project  to kind of tell the story of of the  stuff that was going on there and it was  a similar Amazon was the worst in that  respect but there was though it was  there were similar things that were true  when I worked in Social Care in  Blackpool w